# 20 — Testing / Safety

- Run focused tests covering changed behavior before claiming completion.
- Include PostgreSQL regression coverage for database-touching changes.
- Verify Alembic has a single head (`alembic heads` yields exactly one revision).
- Run `git diff --check` before finish; whitespace/conflict marker failures are FAIL.
- Report results explicitly as PASS, FAIL, or BLOCKED with exact evidence.
- Do not claim PASS when Docker/PostgreSQL/runtime prerequisites are unavailable.
- Never point automated tests at ERP V2 production databases.
